.SH NAME
le-fix-terminal - Undo terminal modes a killed TUI left behind


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBle fix-terminal [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Undo the terminal modes a TUI leaves behind when it is killed without
getting to clean up — mouse and keyboard reporting, bracketed paste,
a hidden cursor, and the alt screen. Symptoms include a prompt filled with
\fB;62;38M65;…\fR on mouse movement, escape codes from ordinary keys,
a missing cursor, or a terminal that stays
blank after a crash.

.PP
The recovery sequences are safe to repeat. They disable enhanced keyboard
reporting on the active screen, including modes another application may
have enabled. Use this command to recover after a crash. Do not redirect
its output — the escapes must reach the terminal to have any effect.

.PP
\fBreset\fR does this too, and also clears your scrollback.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for fix-terminal


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBle(1)\fP


